# ==============================================================================
# Dygo Academy
# ==============================================================================

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the JWT signing secret, the anon/service_role keys derived from
# it, the Stripe secret key and the VAPID private key. Only .env.example is
# ever committed.
.env
!.env.example

# com.dygoacademy.frontend/.env.local is Next.js's own auto-loaded local-env
# file (holds the Supabase anon key) — unrelated to env-profiles/ below,
# despite the similar-sounding name; see README.md "Running modes" for why
# those are deliberately two different mechanisms.
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# env-profiles/ — the local/stg/prod running-profile overlays (see
# README.md "Running modes: local, dev, production"). Real values are
# gitignored (stg.env carries a personal tailscale IP, prod.env carries
# live Cloudflare R2 credentials); the *.env.example templates alongside
# them are safe placeholders and stay tracked. This folder replaced
# root-level ".env.local" / ".env.stg" / ".env.prod" 2026-09-16 specifically
# because ".env.local" collided, in name only, with the Next.js file above.
env-profiles/*.env
!env-profiles/*.env.example

# R2.readme was found sitting in the repo root holding a live Cloudflare
# API token, Access Key ID and Secret Access Key in plaintext -- not a
# secrets *pattern* so much as one specific leftover file, but excluded by
# name so a future `git add -A` can never pick it up. This file should be
# deleted from disk and those credentials rotated, not just gitignored.
/R2.readme

